 "findings": [
  {
   "finding_id": "V1-001",
   "severity": "high",
   "kind": "contradiction",
   "items": [
    "D-084"
   ],
   "claim": "D-084 makes every Request/Response call after the response completed throw IllegalStateException, which breaks the documented before/after middleware pattern and the onError isCommitted()/abort() pattern required for T37.",
   "evidence": "docs/research/naruserve-v1/design/00.design.md:146; docs/api/middleware.md:90-95 (req.path() after next.run()); docs/api/middleware.md:127-131 and object.md:591-594 (onError reads res.isCommitted() after a possibly completed response); object.md:1069 (T37)",
   "suggested_fix": "Scope the IllegalStateException to use after the request ended (chain and onError returned / connection closed), keep isCommitted()/abort()/read-only accessors legal during the chain and error handling, and keep D-101/D-123 for body/next misuse."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "V1-002",
   "severity": "high",
   "kind": "contradiction",
   "items": [
    "D-335",
    "D-326",
    "D-330",
    "D-327",
    "D-336"
   ],
   "claim": "The SSE design cannot be met on read-only TinyHttpd as written: its EventStream hard-codes Cache-Control: no-cache and cannot emit event/id/retry/data in one block, while the alternative (raw chunked OutputStream) keeps the TinyHttpd worker attached to the pool for the stream lifetime because only EventStream/upgrade detach the worker, starving maxWorkers=64 under T26.",
   "evidence": "/Users/beom/work/git/TinyHttpd/core/src/main/java/com/snoworca/tinyhttpd/server/SseStream.java:53 (Cache-Control no-cache), :68 (pool.detach only here), :72 (commitStreaming), :240 (handler return ends response); /Users/beom/work/git/TinyHttpd/core/src/main/java/com/snoworca/tinyhttpd/http/EventStream.java:24-36; docs/api/sse.md:25,62-67; object.md:458",
   "suggested_fix": "Decide one SSE transport for the TinyHttpd adapter: either accept TinyHttpd EventStream and amend D-326/D-330 (record no-transform and the separate retry block as a deferred TinyHttpd gap under D-020), or use the raw streaming body with a NaruServe-owned bounded queue and a separate SSE thread budget, rewriting D-335/D-336 accordingly."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "V1-003",
   "severity": "medium",
   "kind": "design-gap",
   "items": [
    "D-324",
    "D-336",
    "D-346"
   ],
   "claim": "T26 (100+ concurrent WS and SSE from a local test client) needs TinyHttpd maxConnectionsPerAddress (default 32) and maxEventStreams (default 64) raised; only maxUpgradedConnections is covered.",
   "evidence": "/Users/beom/work/git/TinyHttpd/core/src/main/java/com/snoworca/tinyhttpd/TinyHttpd.java:264,268; /Users/beom/work/git/TinyHttpd/core/src/main/java/com/snoworca/tinyhttpd/server/HttpServer.java:245; /Users/beom/work/git/TinyHttpd/core/src/main/java/com/snoworca/tinyhttpd/server/SseStream.java:60-62 (503 beyond maxEventStreams); object.md:1058",
   "suggested_fix": "Add an item that the adapter configures per-address connection and event-stream limits (and the matching NaruServe settings from D-323/D-339) so the T26 test reaches 100+ connections from loopback."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "V1-004",
   "severity": "low",
   "kind": "design-gap",
   "items": [
    "D-216",
    "D-218",
    "D-225"
   ],
   "claim": "object.md requires header count and wait-queue length to be configurable; design only names header/URL/timeout configuration APIs and keeps header count and queue as TinyHttpd defaults.",
   "evidence": "object.md:829; docs/api/defaults.md:26",
   "suggested_fix": "Extend D-225 to cover header-count and wait-queue configuration APIs (names delegated)."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "V1-005",
   "severity": "medium",
   "kind": "design-gap",
   "items": [
    "D-169",
    "D-371"
   ],
   "claim": "docs/api and object.md make Logcat the default logger on Android; the design only ships a Logcat Logger in a separate artifact and makes console the JVM default, with no item for Android default selection.",
   "evidence": "docs/api/logging.md:78-81; object.md:646",
   "suggested_fix": "Add an item for how Logcat becomes the default on Android (e.g. bootstrap detects the Android artifact via ServiceLoader) or amend docs/api/logging.md to require explicit app.logger(new LogcatLogger())."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "V1-006",
   "severity": "medium",
   "kind": "other",
   "items": [
    "D-002",
    "D-005",
    "D-025",
    "D-179",
    "D-371"
   ],
   "claim": "Internal inconsistency: D-005 says wave 1 declares every module's main dependencies so later waves add only test deps or release plugins, but the SLF4J adapter and rotating file logger modules (D-179, wave 4) and the Android-only Logcat artifact (D-371, wave 8) are not in D-002's wave-1 module list; the Logcat artifact also needs android.jar while D-025 requires the root build to pass without an Android SDK.",
   "evidence": "docs/research/naruserve-v1/design/00.design.md:12,15,43,278,577",
   "suggested_fix": "List the optional logger modules in D-002 (names delegated to #7) and state that the Logcat artifact lives in the samples/android build (or compiles against a Maven android stub), keeping the root build SDK-free."
  },
